<title>USA: Ampal-American swaps class A shares.</title>
<headline>Ampal-American swaps class A shares.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ampal-American Israel Corp said it swapped 3 million shares of its Class A common stock for 3 million shares of its common stock owned by Bank Hapoalim.</p>
<p>The company said the swap means it has now only one class of voting stock outstanding.</p>
<p>The company also said it agreed not to reissue any more shares with voting rights preferential to the voting rights of the Class A shares.</p>
<p>Privately held Bank Hapoalim now holds about 5.9 million shares -- or 24.9 percent -- Ampal's stock, Ampal said.</p>
</text>
